%% seq_02c_task_delete.mmd
%% Updated 2026-06-26 (verified).
%% Reader intent: Understand what delete means in runtime terms for a task record.
%% Key boundary: Delete-only flow; restore, archive variants, or downstream cleanup policies are outside this diagram.
%% Current caveat: Runtime behavior is soft-delete, so task history remains important even after removal from active lists.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Project Manager
    participant B as Browser
    participant C as Controller
    participant Cmd as DeleteTaskCommand
    participant Repo as Repository
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Evt as Event Bus

    U->>B: Confirm delete task
    B->>C: DELETE /tasks/:id
    C->>Cmd: execute(dto)
    Cmd->>Cmd: Validate delete permission
    Cmd->>Repo: findById(taskId)
    Repo->>DB: SELECT task
    Repo-->>Cmd: Task aggregate
    Cmd->>Repo: save(task.softDelete)
    Repo->>DB: UPDATE tasks.deleted_at = NOW()
    Cmd->>Evt: emit(task:deleted)
    C-->>B: Redirect to task list
